zuxlsx bundles third-party source code under src/vendor/. Provenance for every
bundled source -- upstream repository, release tag, license and the local
patches applied -- is recorded in tools/vendor/manifest.tsv, with per-file
checksums of the copy as committed in tools/vendor/checksums.sha256.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
xlsxio (src/vendor/xlsxio/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:  https://github.com/brechtsanders/xlsxio
Release:   0.2.36
License:   MIT, reproduced verbatim in src/vendor/xlsxio/LICENSE.txt

  Copyright (c) 2016 Brecht Sanders

Only the XLSX *reader* is bundled: xlsxio_read.c, xlsxio_read_sharedstrings.c
and their headers. The writer (xlsxio_write.c) is deliberately not bundled --
writing workbooks is out of scope (design section 21).

The bundled copy carries one local patch, in tools/patches/xlsxio/:

  0001-miniz-zip-backend.patch  adds a USE_MINIZ backend beside the existing
                                USE_MINIZIP / USE_MINIZIP_NG / libzip ones,
                                so the reader drives miniz's ZIP reader
                                (mz_zip_reader_init_file, _locate_file_v2,
                                _extract_iter_new/_read/_free) instead of
                                requiring system minizip or libzip. Upstream
                                has no miniz backend.

The patch was written in the utopp/pkg-xlsx prototype, not by upstream, and is
reproduced here unchanged. It applies cleanly to the pristine 0.2.36
xlsxio_read.c and reproduces the committed copy byte for byte.

Line endings are CRLF, as shipped by upstream. They are deliberately not
normalised, so the committed bytes still match the release archive.
